That is what the restore utility is for (it restores games after
crashes/power outs etc.).

In my (humble, non-ascended) opinion, taking a backup is always
save-scumming.  Otherwise you start going down a slippery slope, where
you start justifying to yourself that whatever killed you/robbed away
your cool artifact/annoyed you was not your fault, and therefore you
can use your backup.

Your example illustrates this extremely well.  You took an in game
occurrence, a monster being spawned behind a boulder, and judged that
as being "unfair".  But if it's part of the game, then its part of the
game, and any artificial way of going around it is cheating.

Don't kid yourself.  Just Say No... to save-scumming.

